        "id": "part-a",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "a",
        "prompt": "Show that $\\frac{x^2+x}{x^2+4x+3}$ can be written as $\\frac{x}{x+a}$ where $a$ is a positive integer.",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$a=3$",
          "worked": "Factor numerator and denominator and cancel $(x+1)$: the expression is $\\frac{x}{x+3}$.",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": null
      },
      {
        "id": "part-b",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "b",
        "prompt": "Hence, given $f(x) = \\frac{x^2+x}{x^2+4x+3}$, find an expression for $f^{-1}(x)$.",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$\\frac{3x}{1-x}$",
          "worked": "From $y=\\frac{x}{x+3}$, rearrange $yx+3y=x$ to get $x(1-y)=3y$, so $x=\\frac{3y}{1-y}$.",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": null
      }
    ]
  },
